/* ================= v27 admin: administrative units and their seats of government (★) =================
   Real maps (Singapore, SF Bay Area, New York City): a star at the real government building of each unit, with the unit's
   name; bigger units get bigger stars (a double ring for the nation / New York City, a ring for CDC districts, counties and
   boroughs). The stars are labels of the app's label layer (screen-space decluttering by priority, distance limits by size).
   Hover or click a star: the unit's outline is drawn on the ground and a small bilingual card shows the level, population and
   the government building. Data: lm24/admin/mkdata.py (OSM townhalls and admin boundaries; Singapore CDC addresses).
   Generated cities (示例城市 / new island): the star sits on the city's city hall (the capital gets the double ring); the city
   label and centre follow it; with no city hall the star is hollow at the label position. The district pane shows the seat.
   Test handle: window.SGAdmin. Hooks: wraps syncLabels / renderDistrictList (no main-code patch needed). */
